WEBVTT

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.150
The Price of Smiles

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.150
<i>The Price of Smiles</i>

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:36.400
<b><i>The Price of Smiles</i></b>

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:38.620
They're not the Order.

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:39.780
A margrave army, maybe?

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:42.160
You think they're deserting?

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.040
That's the old Verde territory ahead...

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.310
We can't let them escape!

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:54.050
I guess we can't shake them off.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:57.070
You go on. We'll hold them off.

00:01:58.990 --> 00:01:59.980
Princess Yuki.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.440
Get away from the window.

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:03.520
O-Okay.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:11.240
Hey. Wasn't that...

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:14.690
Damn it!

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:18.570
Initiating attack!

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:21.700
Lily, go right! 
I'll go left and head them off!

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:23.700
Hang on! I'm on my way!

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.850
Lune, what's our position?

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:29.940
Ninety kilometers to the 
old Empire of Verde territory.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:33.660
If we manage to shake them off, we can 
reach our destination by midnight.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:35.580
I see...

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.190
Increase our speed to maximum.

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:40.090
We need to get there as quickly as possible.

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:45.620
I'm sorry.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:49.600
We were hoping to capture a 
pilot for questioning, but...

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:51.380
They were fighting tooth and nail,

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.390
so we couldn't hold back, either...

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:54.860
The result is plain to see.

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:56.740
Why would they be so desperate?

00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:59.570
It's odd behavior for a rural squadron...

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:02.820
Hey... what do you think of this?

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:05.450
Hey! This is...

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:12.910
Yuki Soleil, Princess of 
the Kingdom of Soleil.

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:14.010
I'm sure of it.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:15.360
But why?

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:18.150
Shouldn't the princess be leading 
the big face-off right now?

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:20.510
You think she's abandoning her people?

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:23.770
If so, it's unforgivable!

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:27.510
Doesn't she care at all about 
the soldiers on the front lines?

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:31.640
Anyway, I'll make the report.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:40.360
What's that? Yuki Soleil?

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:41.480
Yes.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:45.440
The data analyst says it's 
extremely likely to be her.

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:49.080
Where was she sighted?

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:49.790
Put it on.

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:54.510
That region...

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:59.180
Going north would take them to the 
experimental facility in the Empire of Verde.

00:03:59.180 --> 00:03:59.880
Indeed.

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:04.080
If it really could shut down chrars at will,

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:06.230
its military value would be incalculable.

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:11.120
That is why our empire did 
not dismantle the facility.

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:14.440
At the emperor's command, of course.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:19.800
If the Kingdom has the 
technology to activate it,

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:23.570
and they're able to stop 
only our army's chrars...

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:27.200
The tide would be turned immediately.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.920
Form a dragnet.

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:31.950
Find the princess at any cost.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.420
Yes, ma'am.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:34.720
Contact all forces.

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:36.460
Begin the full-scale offensive!

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.550
That's all the time we'll 
be buying, I suppose...

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:45.940
Return fire!

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:47.750
They have an overwhelming material advantage.

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:50.560
Don't engage them head-on! 
Draw out the fighting as long as you can!

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:51.470
Sir!

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.040
Is the main battle still going?

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:07.990
Yeah, it's been four hours now.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:11.490
The Kingdom's really hanging in there, huh?

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.120
Here and here...

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:16.130
And this is the last place 
a sighting was reported.

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:18.280
All their theurgears have been destroyed.

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:21.000
The last image is just the two vehicles.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:23.560
So they didn't bring any other squads?

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:27.010
Pretty light guard for a 
princess, don't you think?

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:29.900
I just got our orders.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:33.110
We're to go north and enter the 
old Empire of Verde territory.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:36.480
But there's nothing up there!

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:38.980
Break's over! Let's go.

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:42.240
Hey.

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:46.490
This is...

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:48.570
I just happened to find it.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:50.300
It's like a good luck charm for you, right?

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:51.370
Not good to be without it...

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:55.450
I couldn't sleep at night 
if you died on me first.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:02.960
<b>Old Verde Territory</b>

00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:13.140
Lune here. Nothing in the area.

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:15.590
Roger. Stay on guard there.

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:22.900
This is the Empire of Verde's 
experimental facility.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:25.190
I don't see any damage.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:27.820
It might just...

00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:35.410
We're hooking up the new chrars units.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:38.650
Based on the data Lord Izana sent us,

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:42.850
I matched the unit model to the old 
Imperial standard before we left.

00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:49.430
It should finally let the facility 
execute its original purpose.

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:53.930
Miss Layla... you really 
were a chrars researcher...

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:56.040
It's ironic.

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:58.930
I thought I'd forgotten all of this.

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:01.940
I'll be fine.

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:04.350
Beginning energy distribution.

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:19.320
What's with that light?

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:21.140
Looks like we found 'em...

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:24.370
<i>An Order machine?</i>

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:25.870
<i>Where'd it even come from?</i>

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:27.550
<i>Is that it? Just that one?</i>

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:28.710
<i>I can't be sure.</i>

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:31.220
Let's wait for reinforcements.

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:33.570
There could be others lying in wait.

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:35.000
<i>Sounds smart to me.</i>

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:37.440
<i>No, we're all going to charge in at once.</i>

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:40.170
We have a direct order 
from Chief of Staff Eine:

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:43.080
"Stop the princess, even if 
it costs you your lives."

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:43.740
Why?!

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:45.120
Who knows?

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:47.700
We're just disposable pawns to them anyway.

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:49.440
I'll take the lead.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:50.320
You support me.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:51.490
Stella!

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:53.660
You idiot! After all that 
crap you said to me...

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:54.640
<i>Don't worry.</i>

00:07:55.430 --> 00:07:56.990
<i>I won't throw my life away.</i>

00:07:58.280 --> 00:08:00.010
Let's all live through this.

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:01.910
Initiating plan!

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:02.710
Let's go!

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:03.860
Roger!

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:10.250
<i>The enemy have found us.</i>

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:11.310
<i>Hurry up, you guys!</i>

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:12.510
Lune!

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:18.150
More Order machines?

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:19.480
Stella, you stay there!

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:21.640
Huey, go back her up!

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:24.270
Shut up! Don't order me around!

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:35.450
Why, you...!

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:02.730
One enemy has entered the facility!

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:05.850
Princess Yuki, go to the main floor.

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:07.640
Come with me, Miss Layla!

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:10.050
I can't leave just yet.

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:12.070
Go.

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:14.360
You must not waste our faith in you.

00:09:21.730 --> 00:09:24.390
Okay. I'll be waiting upstairs.

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:38.750
Was that...

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:41.330
Generator unit holding stable.

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:42.520
It'll reach critical—

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:02.880
It's no use.

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:05.700
The entire facility is powered now.

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:09.010
What are you people doing—

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:22.970
This facility can shut down chrars at will.

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:25.470
If we shut down the chrars,

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:31.110
our civilization's weapons will 
all become worthless scrap.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:36.610
That is what our ruler, Princess Yuki, wants.

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:39.150
<i>What the princess wants?</i>

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:43.870
<i>It seems unbelievable... 
but if what she's saying is true...</i>

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:49.210
<i>Is she going to use that power 
to destroy the Imperial Army?</i>

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:53.450
<i>That would explain the 
chief of staff's order...</i>

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:58.430
Princess Yuki merely wishes to end the war.

00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:01.620
Even if it means earning the world's censure,

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:03.760
she is prepared to see through her ideals.

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:05.690
<i>Then it's true...</i>

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:07.470
Imperial soldier.

00:11:08.030 --> 00:11:12.710
I know that you, too, have seen many 
terrible sights on the battlefield.

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:17.360
If such things cause you any pain at all...

00:11:58.690 --> 00:11:59.780
I'm so glad...

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:00.920
You...

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:04.120
You survived...

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:10.500
You can't save me.

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:14.630
Don't worry about me.

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:27.030
Princess Yuki... although she acts 
strong, she is still a child.

00:12:28.030 --> 00:12:34.630
Please help her... Help Yuki.

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:39.220
You, who have such kind eyes...

00:12:39.220 --> 00:12:41.820
With her... together...

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:44.070
I know you will...

00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:48.060
bring smiles... to all the 
people of this planet...

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:54.580
My dear... daughters...

00:12:57.780 --> 00:13:00.810
Why... Why did you save me?

00:13:13.490 --> 00:13:15.160
<i>Stop the chrars?</i>

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:18.060
<i>Impossible. It can't be done.</i>

00:13:23.710 --> 00:13:26.020
<i>But if it means...</i>

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:43.920
You're late, Miss Layla—

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:47.140
Who are you?

00:13:47.140 --> 00:13:48.540
What does it matter?

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:51.930
I'm nothing, compared to 
the princess of a country.

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:54.180
Where's Miss Layla?

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:55.870
Did you see her in the room downstairs?

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:58.190
She's important to me!

00:13:59.680 --> 00:14:02.940
That woman... Ah, that person...

00:14:04.850 --> 00:14:07.680
The ceiling came down, and for some reason...

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:09.950
to save me, she...

00:14:18.550 --> 00:14:20.330
She said you plan to stop the chrars.

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:23.210
Are you planning to destroy 
our Imperial Army?

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:27.470
Did Miss Layla tell you that?

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:32.630
Yes. But I'm not doing 
it to defeat the Empire.

00:14:32.630 --> 00:14:36.210
I want to disable all of the world's weapons,

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:38.350
so that we'll never have war again.

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:43.230
I've seen so much of it...

00:14:43.910 --> 00:14:45.990
People dying because of me...

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:49.610
People dying for me...

00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:54.510
I never want it to happen again.

00:14:54.920 --> 00:14:56.370
So I...

00:14:57.180 --> 00:14:59.610
Even if you do get rid of the weapons,

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:01.880
the same thing will happen again.

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:03.130
People will kill each other.

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:05.380
But if we don't do anything,

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:09.530
more and more people will 
die because of the chrars!

00:15:09.530 --> 00:15:11.140
It's not right!

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:15.130
I know. I know it's not that simple,

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:20.140
but I want to believe... 
that humans are good.

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:27.650
That they can stop fighting 
and live together, smiling.

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:32.960
That's just what someone 
raised in a palace would say.

00:15:33.340 --> 00:15:34.910
I can't go along with it.

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:38.600
What would a princess know about our lives?

00:15:39.170 --> 00:15:43.920
About the people forced to spend 
their lives crawling in the dirt?

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:45.670
Stop the chrars, you say?

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:49.120
That's going to shut down 
more than the weapons!

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:52.590
It'll mean losing all the energy 
we need to live our lives!

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:55.300
Not everyone can endure a life like that!

00:15:55.860 --> 00:15:58.180
Things will get harder than they are now!

00:15:58.360 --> 00:16:02.190
But it's better than losing 
more people we care about!

00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:08.230
<i>I don't want to admit it.</i>

00:16:11.720 --> 00:16:12.490
<i>But...</i>

00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:17.080
<i>somewhere in my heart, I've been 
thinking the same thing as her...</i>

00:16:18.020 --> 00:16:23.860
Please help her... Help Yuki.

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:35.260
With passion and will, we can do anything.

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:39.940
That's something... 
someone I loved always said to me.

00:16:40.240 --> 00:16:43.160
I don't care if everyone 
in the world hates me.

00:16:43.530 --> 00:16:46.380
I... I still...

00:16:55.090 --> 00:16:57.780
<i>What do I do? To make a world...</i>

00:16:58.130 --> 00:17:02.580
<i>A world where they don't have to fight...
Where they can smile...</i>

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:09.530
<i>If it's really possible to 
make something like that...</i>

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:16.450
This will really shut them down?

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:18.730
Why...

00:17:18.730 --> 00:17:21.530
The person I owe my life to 
said something to me, too:

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:23.260
"See them through."

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:26.860
I think I'll take my chances

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:28.730
to see what kind of future you'll bring us.

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:32.300
I'll be court-martialed 
for this, to be sure...

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:34.580
What's your name?

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:37.490
Stella.

00:17:38.630 --> 00:17:39.990
Stella Shining.

00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:45.120
Thank you.

00:18:29.310 --> 00:18:31.170
What's going on? Hey!

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:35.550
Princess Yuki...

00:21:04.370 --> 00:21:07.200
Please sign the terms of armistice.

00:21:08.480 --> 00:21:10.030
Summer has come.

00:21:10.320 --> 00:21:13.790
The shutdown of the chrars 
has restored the crops.

00:21:14.440 --> 00:21:18.540
But the world is still in chaos.

00:21:19.640 --> 00:21:23.920
The people who escaped Hariant are 
gradually returning to the city.

00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:31.340
The members of the Buerger Squad 
have all begun walking new paths.

00:21:34.530 --> 00:21:37.020
We've received a request from the Empire.

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:39.850
They're asking if we have any documents 
left from the migration era,

00:21:39.850 --> 00:21:41.190
and if we can make them public.

00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:45.650
It's certainly tempting to go back 
to pre-chrars technology, but...

00:21:45.650 --> 00:21:47.430
We must be as careful as possible.

00:21:47.430 --> 00:21:50.180
We can't afford to make 
the same mistakes again.

00:21:53.750 --> 00:21:56.840
Please, watch over us, everyone.

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:03.870
Regardless of the resentments 
of the past, just as you wished,

00:22:04.770 --> 00:22:07.090
we're going to live on, hand in hand.

00:22:08.380 --> 00:22:09.560
Welcome!

00:22:09.560 --> 00:22:12.230
Thanks for coming all this way!

00:22:13.470 --> 00:22:14.560
What's this?

00:22:14.770 --> 00:22:15.980
It's weird!

00:22:16.270 --> 00:22:17.840
Cute, isn't it?

00:22:17.840 --> 00:22:20.910
Yeah, it is! I want one, too!

00:22:21.620 --> 00:22:22.480
Um...

00:22:22.900 --> 00:22:26.850
Thank you for your intervention 
with the military command.

00:22:27.590 --> 00:22:28.990
You mean, about Stella?

00:22:29.230 --> 00:22:30.160
Yes.

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:33.490
Her punishment was minimal, thanks to you.

00:22:33.790 --> 00:22:36.500
She's off doing service 
with the security team now

00:22:36.500 --> 00:22:38.810
because they're so short-handed...

00:22:38.810 --> 00:22:40.240
Here, a thank-you.

00:22:40.240 --> 00:22:42.050
Enjoy it with the children.

00:22:42.050 --> 00:22:43.190
Not at all.

00:22:44.560 --> 00:22:46.350
And thank you, as always.

00:22:53.490 --> 00:22:54.870
It's been a long time.

00:22:54.870 --> 00:22:57.140
Thank you for talking to the army for me.

00:22:57.860 --> 00:23:01.770
Well, we need you to see 
them through, after all.

00:23:04.300 --> 00:23:05.810
That reminds me...

00:23:05.810 --> 00:23:06.650
Yes.

00:23:07.630 --> 00:23:09.240
They're blooming beautifully, aren't they?

00:23:10.720 --> 00:23:12.160
Ours are, too.

00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:19.440
<i>This is the story of two girls...</i>

00:23:20.590 --> 00:23:21.960
<i>...born on a planet...</i>

00:23:30.840 --> 00:23:32.740
<i>...far, far away.</i>
